    "modelReasoning": "The policy limits how often arrivals exceed 20, which is a tail probability. Arrivals from n independent bookings with 85% attendance are binomial. At 23 bookings the mean is 19.55, but P(X > 20) is 0.31. The largest n with P(X > 20) at or below 0.05 is 21 (0.033). Booking 20 also meets the policy but leaves chairs empty; 22 gives 0.137. Confirm with a simulation."
